1
00:00:00,650 --> 00:00:03,659
Which plan still feeds people when a vehicle fails?

2
00:00:03,659 --> 00:00:08,675
FORK lets a coordinator test that decision before dispatch, with a synthetic mission.

3
00:00:10,650 --> 00:00:16,518
This food bank has two hundred forty meals, two hundred sixty four requested, and three vehicles.

4
00:00:16,518 --> 00:00:21,236
Each strategy receives an isolated copy of the same resources and constraints.

5
00:00:22,650 --> 00:00:27,969
Velocity, Resilience, and Equity express different priorities in a deterministic planner.

6
00:00:27,969 --> 00:00:34,005
Ordinary greedy routing delivers two hundred twenty four meals initially, beating every named policy.

7
00:00:34,005 --> 00:00:35,738
FORK keeps that loss visible.

8
00:00:38,650 --> 00:00:42,096
Now vehicle A fails at minute twenty five in every world.

9
00:00:42,096 --> 00:00:44,272
Completed deliveries stay completed.

10
00:00:44,272 --> 00:00:45,784
Its cargo stays stranded.

11
00:00:45,784 --> 00:00:48,444
Recovery can change only the remaining plan.

12
00:00:51,650 --> 00:00:55,495
All three adapted plans now deliver one hundred sixty eight meals.

13
00:00:55,495 --> 00:01:02,835
With fixed routes under the same failure, they deliver one hundred forty four, one hundred twenty, and one hundred forty four.

14
00:01:02,835 --> 00:01:05,631
This measures recovery against a paired control.

15
00:01:08,650 --> 00:01:11,387
Better depends on the coordinator's priorities.

16
00:01:11,387 --> 00:01:15,406
Adjust the weights for coverage, high need service, and modeled cost.

17
00:01:15,406 --> 00:01:20,357
The comparison uses verified outcomes and reports ties instead of inventing a winner.

18
00:01:21,650 --> 00:01:27,030
A separate referee reconstructs movement, cargo, and timing, then recomputes the metrics.

19
00:01:27,030 --> 00:01:30,475
Its receipt checks consistency inside the declared model.

20
00:01:30,475 --> 00:01:33,860
It does not prove route optimality or real world safety.

21
00:01:36,650 --> 00:01:39,936
A person reviews the evidence and approves this revision.

22
00:01:39,936 --> 00:01:43,855
The exported packet carries the simulated plan and its verification.

23
00:01:43,855 --> 00:01:45,123
Nothing is dispatched.

24
00:01:45,123 --> 00:01:50,254
FORK makes the tradeoffs inspectable, and leaves the final decision with the coordinator.
